# Inactive whole-plan restoration guard

Default POLICY_SHA256 is PENDING; root alone may adopt an independently reviewed policy later.
`checked` needs explicit supplied prior bytes and returns policy plus fully restored .11 contract/plan.
It restores and whole-checks .11 before unchanged old G checks every original rule, hold and source fragment.
It then rebuilds the exact current .12 objects, rejecting coherent policy/child/parent/graph tampering.
Prior reader must provide whole-bound .11 generator/schema/source bytes; it never substitutes current changed source.
Current proposed generator and fixed child inputs remain independently bound explicit byte claims.
No loader, constructor, seal, execution lease or native/UI/backend-restart acceptance follows.
